PARITY SUMMARY
  The web WeekSelector is a controlled `GlassPanel` row driven by `useWeeklyDigest`:
    [ Button ghost sm  ◂ Previous ]   [ 🗓  {weekLabel}  {isCurrentWeek && <Badge info>Current</Badge>} ]
                                                                                 [ Next ▸  ghost sm, disabled@current ]
  Props: weekLabel:string · isCurrentWeek:boolean · onPrevWeek() · onNextWeek(). `weekLabel` is pure
  date math (web `useMemo`: `getWeekRange(offset)` → Monday-of-week + offset·7 days, joined
  ``${formatDateShort(start)} – ${formatDateShort(end)}` ``); `isCurrentWeek = weekOffset === 0`;
  `goToNextWeek` is gated on `!isCurrentWeek` (Next never advances past the present); `goToPrevWeek` is
  unbounded backwards.
  Native port reproduces all of it: the prev/label/badge/next bar, the Monday-based range, the
  locale-ordered short-date label (`Jun 3 – Jun 9` for en_US), the `Current` badge on the current week,
  the disabled-Next gate, and the exact three web i18n keys (analytics.weeklyDigest.prevWeek/current/
  nextWeek). Data binds through `WeekSelectorModel` (P1/S8 seam mirroring LoadableState /
  LiveConnectionState); the view performs no HTTP. P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry fires once on appear
  with slug "WeekSelector".
  HIG adaptation (covenant-clean, documented): the web renders BOTH chevrons as leading icons; the
  native bar keeps Previous's chevron leading and moves Next's chevron to the trailing edge — the
  platform-idiomatic pagination affordance the prompt's "native Apple-idiomatic" mandate calls for
  ("Do not port web Tailwind classes — use platform tokens"). Composition (a directional chevron + its
  directional label + the badge) and every i18n key are preserved; only the icon side differs.

STATES (every state renders — the navigation bar is ALWAYS present, never hidden behind a null guard;
the digest chrome is layered under it so the selector stays usable in every state — the correct UX for a
navigation control, and the same "native chrome around the web core" pattern accepted for sibling 0035)
  loading  → the bar + a one-line skeleton chrome (the digest summary loading while the queries resolve)
  content  → the bar (label + Current badge on the current week); no extra chrome
  empty    → the bar + a friendly "No drives or charges recorded this week" hint (web `hasData === false`)
  error    → the bar + an inline QueryError-equivalent with a Retry affordance (navigation stays usable)
  stale    → a freshness banner above the bar + one guarded auto-refresh, cached label stays visible
  offline  → a freshness banner above the bar ("showing the last loaded week"), cached label visible

